 "text": "- **Domain:** √(x−2) needs x ≥ 2, so the domain is [2, ∞). Option D is the intended answer.\n- **Average speed:** For equal distances, average speed = 2·5·3/(5+3) = 15/4 km/h.\n- **Local government tiers:** This follows the common exam answer of three tiers (Zila, Upazila, Union).\n- **Logic algebra:** It was devised by George Boole.\n- **Seconds pendulum:** Its period is 2 s, so its frequency is 0.5 Hz.\n- **Henna colour:** It comes from lawsone.\n- **Dicot root:** A dicot root has no hypodermis, so \"hypodermis present\" is the wrong statement.\n- **Passive of \"The pill tastes bitter\":** \"The pill is bitter when it is tasted.\"\n- **Translation:** \"Fortunately I could get into the next bus.\"\n- **Screwdriver:** The number of turns depends on the screw's thread pitch, not the handle. Both need the same number of turns; the thicker handle only needs less force.\n- **Central Shaheed Minar:** The architect is Hamidur Rahman.\n- **False statement:** Polarity is a property of covalent compounds, so D is false.\n- **Earthquake damage:** Buildings collapse because of resonance.\n- **Inexorable:** It means \"unyielding\" (অনমনীয়).\n- **Projectile range:** It is maximum at a 45° launch angle.\n\n{\"answers\": {\"000c853a-7896-439c-af8f-83f93a94aa21-146810\": \"D\", \"018777f7-7958-4668-95af-70afe6cf7e66-103354\": \"A\", \"01e79fd1-255b-4857-96fc-59c1f17df04c-15675\": \"A\", \"0269a96c-32f5-477c-bab9-31fd827929f3-51190\": \"C\", \"0328368d-9139-4f5e-b75b-2eae817dba6d-119686\": \"C\", \"034aa277-1099-4156-bd75-02abc0eca393-64103\": \"D\", \"03a5ee94-d39c-4a25-94f3-d20bc8197d6e-141978\": \"C\", \"064a8667-f1ca-4d1a-8459-11db81ef4a69-131760\": \"D\", \"0720a5e2-aa79-49f6-9ed2-98f8473d1fb6-139424\": \"A\", \"084c3183-b891-4cae-bca9-e9b73a923003-48454\": \"C\", \"08bd4ed2-6c89-43d1-91b6-6e7e4695bede-122115\": \"A\", \"08de5d58-d002-429c-ba6c-c49610eea192-102317\": \"D\", \"09255f80-0720-46f4-ae96-f013ca5a79fb-108294\": \"D\", \"09771521-ceb8-449f-bced-46bb53d91cf7